</figure>
<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We perform a statistical analysis of MM-HELIX-100k. The difficulty distribution of MM-HELIX-100k is uniform, with detailed data presented in Tab. <a href="#A1.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ A.4 MM-HELIX-100k Statistics ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ MM-HELIX: Boosting Multimodal Long-Chain Reflective Reasoning with Holistic Platform and Adaptive Hybrid Policy Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>. Additionally, we conduct token length analysis for the questions, answers, and CoTs in MM-HELIX-100k, with the results shown in Tab. <a href="#A1.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ A.4 MM-HELIX-100k Statistics ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ MM-HELIX: Boosting Multimodal Long-Chain Reflective Reasoning with Holistic Platform and Adaptive Hybrid Policy Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.5 </span>Task Difficulty Settings</h3>

<div id="A1.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each task, we divide the difficulty based on different parameters when constructing the initial state of the data. The following is a typical example.</p>
</div>
