<span id="A1.SS6.p29.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_block ltx_minipage ltx_align_top" style="width:208.2pt;">
<span id="A1.SS6.p29.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS6.p29.pic1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Question</span></span>
<span id="A1.SS6.p29.pic1.2.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS6.p29.pic1.2.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Here is a terrain made of bars. Hill: A flat or raised area where the land right before it is lower, and the land right after it is lower too. Valley: A flat or dipped area where the land right before is higher, and the land right after is higher too. Neighboring bars with the same height count as part of the same hill/valley. Calculate the number of hills and valleys. Please provide your answer as an integer.</span></span>
<span id="A1.SS6.p29.pic1.2.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS6.p29.pic1.2.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Reference Answer</span></span>
