<span id="A1.SS6.p31.pic1.2.1.3" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="A1.SS6.p31.pic1.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Difficulty:</span><span id="A1.SS6.p31.pic1.2.1.3.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Level 1</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS6.p31.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_block ltx_minipage ltx_align_top" style="width:208.2pt;">
<span id="A1.SS6.p31.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS6.p31.pic1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Question</span></span>
<span id="A1.SS6.p31.pic1.2.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS6.p31.pic1.2.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Solve this CryptoMath puzzle, where each letter represents a unique digit (0-9). Different letters must correspond to different values, and no leading letter can be zero. Please provide your answer as a list of comma-separated "letter"=number pairs. Example answer format: ["A"=5, "B"=3, … , "Z"=9].</span></span>
<span id="A1.SS6.p31.pic1.2.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS6.p31.pic1.2.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Reference Answer</span></span>
<span id="A1.SS6.p31.pic1.2.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS6.p31.pic1.2.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">["A"=1, "B"=6, "C"=2, "D"=0, "E"=5]</span></span>
</span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
