</span>
<span id="A1.SS6.p32.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_block ltx_minipage ltx_align_top" style="width:208.2pt;">
<span id="A1.SS6.p32.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS6.p32.pic1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Question</span></span>
<span id="A1.SS6.p32.pic1.2.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS6.p32.pic1.2.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">This is a 3x3 Kukurasu puzzle. You need to fill the grid with black cells according to the following rules: 1. The sum of column positions (1 to 3) of black cells in each row must equal the number on the right. 2. The sum of row positions (1 to 3) of black cells in each column must equal the number at the bottom. Please solve the puzzle and provide the solution as a two-dimensional array, using 0 for white cells and 1 for blackcells. Example answer format: [[1, 1, 0], [1, 0, 1], [0, 0, 1]].</span></span>
<span id="A1.SS6.p32.pic1.2.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS6.p32.pic1.2.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Reference Answer</span></span>
<span id="A1.SS6.p32.pic1.2.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS6.p32.pic1.2.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">[[ 0, 0, 1], [1, 1, 0], [1, 0, 0]]</span></span>
</span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
